  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday) \nIssued at 1039 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe synoptic pattern changes little overall heading into Monday, \nalthough convective chances will generally decrease over our \nforecast area as the center of the upper ridge inches farther \nwestward. A few isolated storms may still clip portions of the far\nsouthern TX Panhandle Monday afternoon, but storm chances will be\nmostly confined well to our north. Models remain in good \nagreement that the ridging aloft will build directly overhead \nTuesday before settling more towards the Four Corners region \nWednesday through the end of the week. This will bring another \nperiod of dry weather and triple digit temperatures to most of the\nregion on Tuesday and Wednesday afternoons, with 105 degree or \ngreater high temperatures appearing likely for areas off the \nCaprock. \n\nThursday into the beginning of next weekend, medium range models \ngenerally agree that cyclonic flow aloft will deepen over the \neastern CONUS, which may open the door for a frontal system to pass \nsouthward through the plains states sometime during the late week \nperiod. A few deterministic solutions suggest this may bring a  \nmodest cooldown and increase in precipitation chances Thu-Sat, but \nensemble consensus still overwhelmingly favors a continuation of \nhot and mainly dry weather given the strength of the ridging aloft.",
